WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.620
Wolverine is back, and he's never looked&nbsp;
more like himself – but this classic suit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.160
raises a lot of questions about what's&nbsp;
going on with the X-Men, and the MCU.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.222
"What is this place?"

00:00:10.222 --> 00:00:14.340
Ever since production began on "Deadpool 3,"&nbsp;
rumors surrounding the upcoming threequel have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.360
been going ballistic online. Reports have&nbsp;
suggested a slew of nostalgic cameos are on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.900
the way, including three of the original&nbsp;
X-Men joining Hugh Jackman's Wolverine.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.240
Pair that with the recent news of&nbsp;
Jennifer Garner's return as Elektra,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.140
and "Deadpool 3" is shaping up&nbsp;
to be quite the multiversal story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.686
as the Merc with a Mouth makes his big&nbsp;
debut in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:31.826 --> 00:00:36.300
As if that wasn't exciting enough, Ryan Reynolds&nbsp;
and Hugh Jackman woke up this morning and decided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.020
to break the internet, giving fans the first&nbsp;
official look at Deadpool and Wolverine in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.080
"Deadpool 3." While both heroes are&nbsp;
back and looking better than ever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.680
all eyes are on Jackman as he finally&nbsp;
gets the opportunity to don Wolverine's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.180
iconic yellow suit on the big screen, and it's&nbsp;
just as glorious as anyone could've imagined.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.900
Wolverine's new look for "Deadpool 3" looks&nbsp;
as if he's jumped straight from the pages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.680
of Marvel's "Astonishing X-Men" run, with&nbsp;
Jackman sporting the classic yellow suit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:02.700
with blue accents that look just as vibrant&nbsp;
as they ever did in the comics. Interestingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:07.080
this version features sleeves covering Jackman's&nbsp;
arms, something his comic-book counterpart never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.520
grew accustomed to. The first look also&nbsp;
notably doesn't include Wolverine's iconic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.080
cowl, but given how comic-accurate Jackman's&nbsp;
costume is, it probably isn't far behind him.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.440
While Wolverine's iconic yellow suit&nbsp;
is more than enough to build hype&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.960
for "Deadpool 3," it could also&nbsp;
give fans an idea of what Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.441
Studios plans to do with the X-Men&nbsp;
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:25.441 --> 00:01:29.220
While Jackman's Wolverine may be making&nbsp;
his MCU debut in a blue and gold suit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.720
that doesn't mean he's going to be the MCU's&nbsp;
Wolverine. Reports suggest that Deadpool 3 and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:38.220
other movies in the Multiverse Saga might be more&nbsp;
of a swan song for the Fox X-Men characters - and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.240
if that's the case, we'll probably be getting&nbsp;
a bit of a reset down the line with the MCU's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.960
version of the character. That would likely&nbsp;
mean a whole new actor, and a whole new outfit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:50.460
with the eventual MCU Wolverine maybe taking&nbsp;
on the classic gold and brown suit instead.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:55.500
First introduced in "Uncanny X-Men" #139,&nbsp;
Wolverine's gold and brown suit quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.860
became an iconic design for the character,&nbsp;
wearing it throughout the '80s and early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.000
'90s. In recent years, the costume has&nbsp;
had a resurgence, with Logan wearing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.720
modernized version for the current "X-Men"&nbsp;
run, priming it for a live-action debut.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.040
As for the X-Men, Wolverine's yellow suit&nbsp;
in "Deadpool 3" bodes well for the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:15.240
team. "X-Men" movies of the past decided&nbsp;
to forgo many of the characters' comic book&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:19.260
costumes. Wolverine's new look suggests&nbsp;
that Marvel Studios will likely stick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.135
a little closer to the source material&nbsp;
for the X-Men's suits this time around.

00:02:23.135 --> 00:02:26.640
Now that comic book movies are much more&nbsp;
mainstream than they were twenty years ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.420
it's only natural to showcase the vibrant,&nbsp;
unique costumes that originally made the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:35.040
X-Men staples in the comics industry. Of course,&nbsp;
this is all speculation, but it certainly seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.314
like X-Men fans are in for a treat whenever&nbsp;
the mutants come to the MCU in full force.

00:02:39.314 --> 00:02:42.720
While Deadpool and Wolverine look better&nbsp;
than ever for their upcoming multiversal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.200
buddy cop adventure, Hugh Jackman finally&nbsp;
getting his hands on Wolverine's yellow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.562
suit pays off his long-standing&nbsp;
commitment to bring Logan to life.

00:02:49.562 --> 00:02:53.820
Over 20 years ago, when "X-Men" first hit&nbsp;
theaters, it infamously threw out the characters'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:58.320
vibrant colors, choosing to style everyone&nbsp;
in a uniformed black leather look instead.

00:02:58.495 --> 00:03:02.836
"What would you prefer? Yellow spandex?"

00:03:02.836 --> 00:03:07.140
While the scene is now iconic, the simple&nbsp;
answer was yes, and fans have been waiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.890
to see their favorite "X-Men" characters&nbsp;
don their classic suits ever since.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:15.840
In Wolverine's case, that day never came -&nbsp;
until "Deadpool 3" hits theaters - but that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.980
didn't stop the studio from teasing Jackman&nbsp;
in the yellow suit. "The Wolverine" filmed an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:24.480
alternate ending featuring Yukio gifting Logan&nbsp;
a yellow and brown suit, but the scene ended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:29.726
up not making the final cut. In an interview&nbsp;
with Screen Rant, director James Mangold said,

00:03:29.726 --> 00:03:32.640
"I somehow feel that if somehow&nbsp;
we ever put Hugh [Jackman] into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.917
one of those outfits, people would not be happy."

00:03:34.917 --> 00:03:36.426
While that may have been the case back then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.426 --> 00:03:41.221
fans seem more than excited to see Jackman&nbsp;
finally get his yellow suit in "Deadpool 3."

